      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "6a73c958f64c57c50e189015",
      "mergedPostDetails": "In VRChat, the groups you join or rep are effectively an extension of your bio.  It's a list of interests, things you find funny, or topics you might be interested in talking about.  \n\nOn a user's in-app full profile page, the current system for the 'groups' card on the full bio places the user's repped group at the top and then shows their remaining shown groups in alphabetical order.  This is wasted space and encourages groups to name themselves starting with numbers or the letter A to be shown \"above the fold\".\n\nInstead, allow users to PIN groups that interest them to the top and show those instead.  this would allow people to feature their interests and topics, which would function as a supplement to the mutual groups feature and help drive social connection.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1878] Allow pinning of groups in your full bio view",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a6ae1858b5f4f581246e871",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Groups are literally used as an interests list in vrchat and being able to display the ones more relevant to your interests is a major way of finding new and interesting places to hang out as well as new people you might have otherwise overlooked. Being able to choose which ones you display is already a core part of vrchat, now please give us the ability to pin five groups to our bio instead of displaying the top alphabetical ones. Already 90% the time all I see is --GROUP-- names or \"18+ verified\" (group name starts with numeric and goes to the top) which is redundant information at best.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
